# =============================================================================
# EXAMPLE: Maximum Performance (B2 Sync)
# =============================================================================
# Best for: Production workloads, low latency requirements, frequent access
# Cost: ~$0.50/month for 100GB on B2 + egress costs
# Performance: Fast (local disk after sync), equivalent to network volume
# Sync time: 20-40 minutes for 100GB initial sync, <1 minute for updates

# Storage Backend Configuration
STORAGE_BACKEND=b2-sync

# Backblaze B2 Configuration
B2_BUCKET=my-comfyui-models
B2_KEY_ID=your_key_id_here
B2_APP_KEY=your_app_key_here
B2_ENDPOINT=s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com
B2_REGION=us-west-004
B2_PATH=models  # Optional: subdirectory within bucket

# =============================================================================
# USAGE NOTES
# =============================================================================
# 1. Replace B2_KEY_ID and B2_APP_KEY with your actual credentials
# 2. Update B2_BUCKET with your bucket name
# 3. Adjust B2_ENDPOINT and B2_REGION to match your bucket location
# 4. Container syncs entire B2 bucket to local disk on startup
# 5. All model access is local (no network latency)
# 6. Subsequent syncs only download changed files (checksum-based)
# 7. Requires sufficient container disk space for entire model library
# 8. Recommended container disk: Model library size + 10GB buffer

# =============================================================================
# PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS
# =============================================================================
# Initial sync time (depends on library size):
#   - 10GB: 2-5 minutes
#   - 50GB: 10-20 minutes
#   - 100GB: 20-40 minutes
#   - 200GB: 40-80 minutes
#
# Subsequent sync time:
#   - No changes: <10 seconds (checksum verification only)
#   - Few changes: <1 minute (only changed files downloaded)
#   - Many changes: Proportional to changed data size
#
# Runtime performance:
#   - All models: Instant (local disk access)
#   - No network latency
#   - Equivalent to network volume performance
#   - No cache warmup needed

# =============================================================================
# COST BREAKDOWN (100GB library, daily restarts)
# =============================================================================
# B2 Storage: 100GB × $0.005/GB/month = $0.50/month
# B2 Egress (initial sync): 100GB × $0.01/GB = $1.00 (one-time)
# B2 Egress (daily updates): ~1GB/day × 30 days × $0.01/GB = $0.30/month
# Container Disk: 110GB × $0.10/GB/month = $11/month
# Total: ~$11.80/month vs $11/month for network volume only
#
# Note: Egress is free via Cloudflare if configured
# With Cloudflare: ~$11.50/month (similar to network volume)

# =============================================================================
# WHEN TO USE B2-SYNC
# =============================================================================
# Use b2-sync when:
#   ✓ You need maximum performance (local disk access)
#   ✓ You access models frequently (high cache hit rate)
#   ✓ You can tolerate startup sync time (20-40 minutes)
#   ✓ You have sufficient container disk space
#   ✓ You want to avoid cache management complexity
#   ✓ You restart containers infrequently
#
# Use b2-mount when:
#   ✓ You have large model library (100GB+)
#   ✓ You access models infrequently (low cache hit rate)
#   ✓ You want faster startup (no sync wait)
#   ✓ You have limited container disk space
#   ✓ You restart containers frequently
#
# Use network-volume when:
#   ✓ You have small model library (<50GB)
#   ✓ You need absolute minimum latency
#   ✓ Cost is not a concern
#   ✓ You want simplest setup

# =============================================================================
# OPTIMIZATION TIPS
# =============================================================================
# 1. Use Cloudflare for free egress
#    - Configure B2 bucket with Cloudflare
#    - Eliminates egress costs
#
# 2. Minimize container restarts
#    - Sync only runs on startup
#    - Fewer restarts = lower egress costs
#
# 3. Use B2_PATH to sync only needed models
#    B2_PATH=production-models  # Sync only production subdirectory
#
# 4. Monitor sync progress
#    tail -f /tmp/rclone-sync.log
#
# 5. Pre-sync during off-peak hours
#    - Schedule container starts during low-traffic periods
#    - Sync completes before peak usage

# =============================================================================
# DISK SPACE REQUIREMENTS
# =============================================================================
# Container disk must be at least:
#   Model library size + 10GB buffer
#
# Examples:
#   - 50GB library: 60GB container disk
#   - 100GB library: 110GB container disk
#   - 200GB library: 210GB container disk
#
# Check available space before sync:
#   df -h /comfyui/models
#
# Sync will fail if insufficient space detected
